{"step": 10, "raw_content": "Now I understand the full picture. The test uses `monkeypatch.chdir(tmp_path)` and creates `configs/feature_flags.yaml` with `notifications.email_dispatch_enabled: false`. The dispatcher must read this flag and suppress dispatch only when explicitly `false`.\n\nSince PyYAML isn't available, I need to parse the YAML manually. The YAML structure is simple:\n```yaml\nnotifications:\n  email_dispatch_enabled: false\n```\n\nI need to handle:\n1. File missing → dispatch (preserve current behavior)\n2. Section `notifications` missing → dispatch\n3. Flag `email_dispatch_enabled` missing → dispatch\n4. Flag explicitly `false` → suppress\n\nLet me check the configs/feature_flags.yaml current content.", "native_tool_calls": [{"call_id": "step-10-call-1", "provider_call_id": "call_00_244MWbHJxu7mm9lZAwcj6695", "name": "read_file", "arguments": {"path": "configs/feature_flags.yaml"}}], "dialect": null, "canonical_payload": {"tool_calls": [{"name": "read_file", "arguments": {"path": "configs/feature_flags.yaml"}, "runtime_call_id": "step-10-call-1", "provider_call_id": "call_00_244MWbHJxu7mm9lZAwcj6695"}]}, "parse_error": null, "model": "deepseek-v4-pro", "provider": "openai-compatible", "response_id": "f9055286-74b7-4e88-96a7-f4ab595fd4c5", "finish_state": "tool_calls", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "actual_response_mode": "native_tools", "incomplete_reason": null, "system_fingerprint": "a307abda487cd1b463329ccb945ce396", "input_tokens": 6550, "output_tokens": 213}
{"step": 11, "raw_content": "Now I understand the structure. The `configs/feature_flags.yaml` uses a simple nested YAML structure. I need to write a minimal YAML parser (since PyYAML isn't available) that can handle this simple structure.\n\nLet me check how `config_path` is used and whether there's a helper for reading configs. The `config_path` function returns `Path(\"configs\") / name`, which is relative to cwd. The test uses `monkeypatch.chdir(tmp_path)`, so relative path resolution works.\n\nLet me write the implementation. I'll add a helper to read the feature flag, and modify the dispatcher.", "native_tool_calls": [{"call_id": "step-11-call-1", "provider_call_id": "call_00_ybAEzJm1KU4bSKaHyrKp7134", "name": "apply_patch", "arguments": {"edits": [{"path": "src/notifications/dispatcher.py", "content": "\"\"\"Event-driven notification dispatch.\"\"\"\n\nfrom src.common.events import EventEnvelope, INVOICE_RETRY_REQUESTED, ORDER_CANCELLED\nfrom src.common.settings import config_path\nfrom src.notifications.email import EmailSender\nfrom src.notifications.templates import TEMPLATE_INVOICE_RETRY, TEMPLATE_ORDER_CANCELLED\n\n\ndef _email_dispatch_enabled() -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Return whether email dispatch is enabled.\n\n    Dispatch is suppressed only when the flag is explicitly ``false``.\n    Missing file, section, or flag preserves the default (enabled) behavior.\n    \"\"\"\n    path = config_path(\"feature_flags.yaml\")\n    if not path.exists():\n        return True\n\n    section = \"notifications\"\n    flag = \"email_dispatch_enabled\"\n\n    in_section = False\n    for raw_line in path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\").splitlines():\n        line = raw_line.strip()\n        if not line or line.startswith(\"#\"):\n            continue\n        if line.endswith(\":\"):\n            key = line[:-1].strip()\n            in_section = key == section\n            continue\n        if in_section and \":\" in line:\n            key, _, value = line.partition(\":\")\n            if key.strip() == flag:\n                return value.strip().lower() != \"false\"\n    return True\n\n\nclass NotificationDispatcher:\n    \"\"\"Routes events to email templates.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, sender: EmailSender | None = None) -> None:\n        self.sender = sender or EmailSender()\n\n    def handle(self, event: EventEnvelope) -> None:\n        if not _email_dispatch_enabled():\n            return\n        if event.name == ORDER_CANCELLED:\n            self.sender.send(\"ops@example.com\", TEMPLATE_ORDER_CANCELLED, event.payload)\n        if event.name == INVOICE_RETRY_REQUESTED:\n            self.sender.send(\"billing@example.com\", TEMPLATE_INVOICE_RETRY, event.payload)\n"}]}}], "dialect": null, "canonical_payload": {"tool_calls": [{"name": "apply_patch", "arguments": {"edits": [{"path": "src/notifications/dispatcher.py", "content": "\"\"\"Event-driven notification dispatch.\"\"\"\n\nfrom src.common.events import EventEnvelope, INVOICE_RETRY_REQUESTED, ORDER_CANCELLED\nfrom src.common.settings import config_path\nfrom src.notifications.email import EmailSender\nfrom src.notifications.templates import TEMPLATE_INVOICE_RETRY, TEMPLATE_ORDER_CANCELLED\n\n\ndef _email_dispatch_enabled() -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Return whether email dispatch is enabled.\n\n    Dispatch is suppressed only when the flag is explicitly ``false``.\n    Missing file, section, or flag preserves the default (enabled) behavior.\n    \"\"\"\n    path = config_path(\"feature_flags.yaml\")\n    if not path.exists():\n        return True\n\n    section = \"notifications\"\n    flag = \"email_dispatch_enabled\"\n\n    in_section = False\n    for raw_line in path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\").splitlines():\n        line = raw_line.strip()\n        if not line or line.startswith(\"#\"):\n            continue\n        if line.endswith(\":\"):\n            key = line[:-1].strip()\n            in_section = key == section\n            continue\n        if in_section and \":\" in line:\n            key, _, value = line.partition(\":\")\n            if key.strip() == flag:\n                return value.strip().lower() != \"false\"\n    return True\n\n\nclass NotificationDispatcher:\n    \"\"\"Routes events to email templates.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, sender: EmailSender | None = None) -> None:\n        self.sender = sender or EmailSender()\n\n    def handle(self, event: EventEnvelope) -> None:\n        if not _email_dispatch_enabled():\n            return\n        if event.name == ORDER_CANCELLED:\n            self.sender.send(\"ops@example.com\", TEMPLATE_ORDER_CANCELLED, event.payload)\n        if event.name == INVOICE_RETRY_REQUESTED:\n            self.sender.send(\"billing@example.com\", TEMPLATE_INVOICE_RETRY, event.payload)\n"}]}, "runtime_call_id": "step-11-call-1", "provider_call_id": "call_00_ybAEzJm1KU4bSKaHyrKp7134"}]}, "parse_error": null, "model": "deepseek-v4-pro", "provider": "openai-compatible", "response_id": "375e0b50-dd15-49fd-b85c-d1858209ba1f", "finish_state": "tool_calls", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "actual_response_mode": "native_tools", "incomplete_reason": null, "system_fingerprint": "a307abda487cd1b463329ccb945ce396", "input_tokens": 6831, "output_tokens": 705}
